---
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/latin-200.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/latin-300.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/latin-300.css';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Version from '../components/Version.astro';
import { breadcrumbs, website } from '../seo/jsonld';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Methodology · Scintille"
	description="How Scintille gets lightning from orbit to the globe: sources, live pipeline, Iceberg lakehouse, storm catalog, stack and limits."
	jsonLd={[
		website(),
		breadcrumbs([
			{ name: 'Scintille', path: '/' },
			{ name: 'Methodology', path: '/methodology/' },
		]),
	]}
>
	<main class="method">
		<a class="name" href="/">Scintille</a>
		<h1>Methodology</h1>
		<p class="lead">Lightning seen from orbit, on the globe minutes later.</p>

		<h2 id="pipeline">Pipeline</h2>
		<div class="flow">
			<section>
				<h3>Live · seconds</h3>
				<ol>
					<li><b>Satellites</b>GLM file every 20 s, LI every 10 min</li>
					<li><b>ingest-live</b>Polls, parses, dedupes</li>
					<li><b>Live feed</b>30 s chunks on R2, last hour</li>
					<li><b>Globe</b>Plays 2 min behind real time</li>
				</ol>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h3>Lake · minutes to hours</h3>
				<ol>
					<li><b>Spool</b>Each batch on disk first</li>
					<li><b>lake-writer</b>Iceberg commit every 5 min</li>
					<li><b>Dagster</b>Gold tables and storms, hourly</li>
					<li><b>Replays</b>Storm catalog on R2</li>
				</ol>
			</section>
		</div>

		<h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>NOAA GOES-East and GOES-West lightning mappers (GLM): the Americas. Listed every 10 s on AWS open data.</li>
			<li>EUMETSAT MTG Lightning Imager (LI): Europe, Africa, the Atlantic. Checked every 30 s on the EUMETSAT Data Store.</li>
			<li>Clouds: hourly composite of GOES, Himawari and MTG full disks, gaps filled by NOAA GMGSI. Cloud-top heights come from the infrared and the GFS temperature profile.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Where two satellites overlap, the one with the better view draws the flash.</p>

		<h2 id="delay">Near real time</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>A GLM file lands about 30 s after the flash; the feed publishes every 30 s.</li>
			<li>The globe plays 2 min behind, so every flash is loaded before it is due.</li>
			<li>LI ships 10 minute files: Europe and Africa play 12 min behind.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Live delay per satellite is on the <a href="/status/">status page</a>.</p>

		<h2 id="lakehouse">Lakehouse</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Apache Iceberg tables on Cloudflare R2, behind R2 Data Catalog.</li>
			<li>Bronze: one row per satellite file. Silver: one row per flash, by day and source. Gold: hourly stats and storms.</li>
			<li>The live feed never waits for the lake: a catalog outage only grows the spool.</li>
			<li>Idempotent: flash ids hash their source file, so a replay writes nothing twice.</li>
			<li>Backfills rebuild a whole day from the upstream archives.</li>
			<li>Blocking quality checks on every gold table.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="storms">Storm catalog</h2>
		<ol class="steps">
			<li>Flashes within 10 km and 10 min cluster into cells (ST-DBSCAN), stuck pixels removed.</li>
			<li>Cells link hour to hour into storms, with splits and merges.</li>
			<li>A level from flash count and peak rate, Light to Exceptional.</li>
			<li>A place name, looked up offline: "Ajaccio, Corsica, France".</li>
			<li>Strong storms and above are published with their replay.</li>
		</ol>
		<p>Runs every hour: a storm can be replayed within about 80 min. Storms active now refresh every 5 min.</p>

		<h2 id="stack">Stack</h2>
		<ul class="stack">
			<li><b>Ingest</b>Python, asyncio</li>
			<li><b>Lake</b>Iceberg, PyIceberg, DuckDB SQL</li>
			<li><b>Orchestration</b>Dagster, Postgres</li>
			<li><b>Runtime</b>Docker Compose on one VPS</li>
			<li><b>Edge</b>Cloudflare R2 and Workers, Astro</li>
			<li><b>Globe</b>Three.js, WebGL</li>
			<li><b>Infra</b>Terraform, GitHub Actions</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="storage">Storage</h2>
		<p>Sized for the R2 free tier: 10 GB and a million writes a month.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Live feed: last hour.</li>
			<li>Flashes: 21 days.</li>
			<li>Storm replays: 60 days. Storm summaries and gold tables: kept.</li>
			<li>Cloud frames: 30 days, their 1 km detail one day.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="coverage">Coverage</h2>
		<p>
			Asia, Oceania and the poles have no lightning feed yet and are shaded. Detection also weakens towards the edge
			of each view. An empty region is not a region without lightning.
		</p>

		<h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Satellites miss some flashes.</li>
			<li>Brightness ranks each flash within its satellite: GLM and LI measure light differently.</li>
			<li>A faulty detector pixel can flash in place.</li>
			<li>Clouds are hourly and lag the lightning.</li>
			<li>Close up, cloud thickness, texture and transparency are styled within stated bounds: satellites only see where clouds are and how high their tops reach. The densest clouds are drawn 95 % opaque, but lightning under them is dimmed only as much as 80 % would, so it shows through. Shading steepens their slopes up to 1.6 times, and up to 2.4 times on dense tops under a high sun, whose light barely changes with slope; at that hour broad decks are also lit as if the sun were lower, their measured shape drawn 6 times steeper. Seen from farther, dense clouds are shaded from their measured tops smoothed to the scale of the screen, slopes drawn up to 12 times steeper and lit by the sun with the contrast of a sun at most 40° high; the shadows of taller clouds are computed, not exaggerated. Heights are not exaggerated. Where no height is published, clouds stay flat.</li>
			<li>A flash lights the cloud within its observed footprint at its observed energy: the whole footprint during its pulses, a patch of about two thirds of its radius along the channel between them (styled shape, observed extent and energy), shaped by the drawn cloud columns, and kept at 35 % over sunlit cloud (a styled trace: nothing of a flash shows by day); overlapping flashes keep the brightest, never add up.</li>
			<li>The ground is a composite: 2004 by day, 2016 city lights by night.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
		<p class="credits">
			GLM data courtesy of NOAA.<br />
			Contains modified EUMETSAT Meteosat data 2026.<br />
			Clouds: NOAA GOES-East and GOES-West, JMA Himawari-9 via NOAA, contains modified EUMETSAT Meteosat data 2026; gaps from NOAA NESDIS GMGSI.<br />
			Earth imagery: NASA Earth Observatory.<br />
			Storm names: GeoNames (CC BY 4.0), Natural Earth.<br />
			Sound: CC0 recordings from Freesound.
		</p>
		<Version />
	</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.method {
		--ink: rgb(238 242 247 / 0.9);
		--soft: rgb(238 242 247 / 0.62);
		--dim: rgb(238 242 247 / 0.4);
		--hair: rgb(238 242 247 / 0.14);
		--mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
		--sans: 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
		max-width: 34rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: clamp(24px, 6vw, 72px) 16px 96px;
		color: var(--soft);
		font: 300 15px/1.75 var(--sans);
		-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
	}
	.name {
		color: var(--ink);
		font: 200 18px/1 var(--sans);
		letter-spacing: 0.5em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	h1 {
		margin: 56px 0 0;
		color: var(--dim);
		font: 300 10px/1 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.24em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	.lead {
		margin: 16px 0 0;
		color: var(--ink);
		font: 200 22px/1.5 var(--sans);
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 48px 0 10px;
		color: var(--dim);
		font: 300 10px/1 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.24em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	p,
	ul,
	ol {
		margin: 0 0 10px;
	}
	ul,
	.steps {
		padding-left: 14px;
	}
	.steps li::marker {
		color: var(--dim);
		font: 300 11px/1 var(--mono);
	}
	a {
		color: var(--ink);
		text-decoration-color: var(--hair);
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
	}
	.flow {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 24px;
	}
	.flow h3 {
		margin: 0 0 12px;
		color: var(--dim);
		font: 300 9.5px/1 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
	}
	.flow ol {
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.flow li {
		position: relative;
		padding: 0 0 18px 16px;
		border-left: 1px solid var(--hair);
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}
	.flow li:last-child {
		padding-bottom: 0;
		border-left-color: transparent;
	}
	.flow li::before {
		position: absolute;
		top: 6px;
		left: -3px;
		width: 5px;
		height: 5px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		content: '';
		background: var(--soft);
	}
	.flow b,
	.stack b {
		display: block;
		color: var(--ink);
		font: 300 11px/1.6 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
	}
	.stack {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(9.5rem, 1fr));
		gap: 14px 24px;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}
	.credits {
		color: var(--dim);
		font: 300 11px/1.8 var(--mono);
	}
	:focus-visible {
		outline: 1px solid var(--soft);
		outline-offset: 5px;
	}
	@media (max-width: 420px) {
		.flow {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
